{"parentUuid":"9575a259-09e7-4e73-b6a0-b0386f52eeff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Qtg59dn3yC2LNNYNCWtqRg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All clean.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe reviewer is correct. I confirmed the bug by inspecting `cobra@v1.10.2`:\n\n- `SetHelpCommand` only stores the command on the struct (`command.go:338`).\n- `InitDefaultHelpCmd` is what actually adds it to the tree, and it runs from `ExecuteC` (`command.go:1100`) — after `MaybeRunPlugin`.\n- Same lazy pattern applies to the default `completion` command (`InitDefaultCompletionCmd`, called at `command.go:1113`).\n\nA small repro verified that `Find([\"help\"])` pre-`Execute` returns `cmd == rootCmd, err = \"unknown command \"help\" for \"entire\"\"`. Since the existing guard requires `err == nil && cmd != rootCmd`, it never fires for `help`, and an `entire-help` binary on PATH would shadow the built-in.\n\n**Fix** (`cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go:79-86`): prime `InitDefaultHelpCmd` and `InitDefaultCompletionCmd` before calling `Find`. Both are idempotent — Cobra calls them again inside `Execute` with no harm.\n\n**Regression tests** (`cmd/entire/cli/plugin_test.go`): added `TestResolvePlugin_BuiltinHelpWins` (covers `help` and `help session`) and `TestResolvePlugin_BuiltinCompletionWins`. Confirmed both fail on the unpatched code and pass with the fix. Full `cmd/entire/cli` suite + lint pass.\n\n(Out of scope: the hidden `__complete` command is initialized via the unexported `initCompleteCmd` and can't be primed externally — it's effectively unreachable as a plugin name in practice since users don't type `__complete`.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":91653,"output_tokens":612,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens"